onsibility. We have some facts: Candidate A puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills (mentioned in SMM). Also we have note: \"Puts concern for others above everything; excellent attention skills\". Not yet discussed. We can bring that up to strengthen A. Also we could ask about Candidate B's crew cooperation and adaptability, but we already asked and got no info. Could ask about Candidate C's health concerns? Not in notes. Actually we have no health note for C. The note says \"unhealthy eating habits\"? Not in our notes. Actually the notes we have: \"Candidate C is regarded as a show-off\" and \"not open to new ideas\". No health. So we can bring up that C is regarded as a show-off and not open to new ideas, which are concerns for crew cooperation and adaptability. Also D's moody and loner. So we can reinforce A.\n\nThus we will state we continue to recommend Candidate A, adding evidence: A's excellent attention skills and concern for others, which support responsibility and attention to detail. Also note that A's communication difficulty is a concern but can be mitigated.\n\nWe should reference prior discussion: agree with Agent 1 and Agent 3. Provide new evidence: \"Puts concern for others above everything\" and \"excellent attention skills\". Also maybe note that A's willingness to further education is low, but we can mitigate with training.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata JSON with vote Candidate A."}
